# Copy to supabase/.env (gitignored). Read by `supabase functions serve`
# (and by `./scripts/dev-up.sh`, which wraps it) - not by the built-in
# edge-runtime container `supabase start` boots on its own, which doesn't
# read this file at all.
#
# SUPABASE_URL / SUPABASE_ANON_KEY / SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are
# auto-injected by the CLI locally, so they don't need to go here.

# Stripe test-mode secret key: https://dashboard.stripe.com/test/apikeys
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_REPLACE_ME

# `./scripts/dev-up.sh` fills this in automatically from `stripe listen`'s
# output. Set by hand only if you're running `stripe listen` yourself:
# `stripe listen --forward-to 127.0.0.1:54321/functions/v1/stripe-webhook`
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_REPLACE_ME

# Optional - only needed to test Telegram "order ready" notifications
# locally. See README.md Part 5 for how to create a bot with @BotFather.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
